{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat any nevelah.</b> Even the nevelah of a clean beast, wild animal, bird, and unclean fish — and the verse rounded them all together, so as not to give an opening to a litigant to object and say: it did not warn against eating nevelah except the nevelah of a clean beast, wild animal, and birds." "<b>Any nevelah.</b> Any nevelah at all — as in ״לא תאכל כל תועבה״, ״לא תעשה כל מלאכה״." "<b>Or sell it to a foreigner.</b> The lamed with a shva." "<b>You shall not boil a kid.</b> It is written here on account of it being meat."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:47.987281036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}